       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults (3,200 mg/day, and usually 2,400 mg/day or less in practice). A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common upper-range anti-inflammatory regimen\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute maximum\n- Something else, such as 1,600 mg total per day split into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Once I have your answer, I'll enter the order."
